From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: allow the Uke mono capture frontend

The Uke capture topology admits one channel, but the component's two-channel
minimum intersects it to an invalid [2,1] interval during PCM open. A bounded
device return probe confirms that ALSA rejects this interval before hw_params.

Lower only the minimum for graph 2 on the explicit Uke microphone card.
Keep the upstream hardware defaults, other cards and all playback limits.
This does not qualify the physical input or change codec electrical settings.

--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
@@ -402,7 +402,13 @@
 	if (substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK)
 		runtime->hw = q6apm_dai_hardware_playback;
-	else if (substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_CAPTURE)
+	else if (substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_CAPTURE) {
 		runtime->hw = q6apm_dai_hardware_capture;
+		/* Match the restricted mono frontend without relaxing other cards. */
+		if (of_machine_is_compatible("xiaomi,uke") && graph_id == 2 &&
+		    of_device_is_compatible(soc_prtd->card->dev->of_node,
+					"xiaomi,uke-microphone-audio-card"))
+			runtime->hw.channels_min = 1;
+	}
 
 	/* Ensure that buffer size is a multiple of period size */
 	ret = snd_pcm_hw_constraint_integer(runtime, SNDRV_PCM_HW_PARAM_PERIODS);
